 uth Campgrounds): https://www.nps.gov/zion/planyourvisit/upload/26-Spring-
 InfoGuide.pdf\n- Pedestrian entrance map and shuttle info: https://www.nps
 .gov/zion/planyourvisit/zion-canyon-shuttle-system.htm\n- Watchman Campgro
 und on Google Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Watchm
 an+Campground+Zion+National+Park\n- South Campground on Google Maps: https
 ://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=South+Campground+Zion+National+
 Park\n- Zion Canyon Visitor Center (south entrance) on Google Maps: https:
 //www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Zion+Canyon+Visitor+Center\n- An
 gels Landing trailhead (The Grotto\, shuttle stop 6) on Google Maps: https
 ://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Grotto+Trailhead+Zion+Natio
 nal+Park\n\nCAMPSITES\n- Watchman Campground (open year-round\, near the s
 outh entrance\, walk to the shuttle). Sites book 6 months ahead: https://w
 ww.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232445 (NPS page: https://www.nps.go
 v/zion/planyourvisit/watchman-campground.htm)\n- South Campground (early M
 arch to October). Only bookable 14 days before arrival: https://www.recrea
